    "body": "## Description\r\n\r\nWhen visiting the `/privacy/firefox/` page I noticed there's a JS error in the console. I believe this is preventing the privacy choices widget from being displayed on the page.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. Visit https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/privacy/firefox/\r\n\r\n### Expected result\r\n\r\nThere's should be a button that offers choice for how Firefox shares data:\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/400117/65317225-54269180-db93-11e9-89ae-b698c4f7d10e.png)\r\n\r\n### Actual result\r\n\r\nThere's no button displayed. Opening the web console, there's a JS error:\r\n\r\n```\r\nTypeError: e[0] is undefined\r\n```\r\n\r\nRunning locally this is a little more descriptive:\r\n\r\n```\r\nTypeError: topicHeaders[0] is undefined\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Environment\r\n\r\nAny browser\r\n",
